{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And every passage of the staff [is] its foundation.</b> A po'al of the heavy doubled binyan, for behold מטה is in feminine language — hear staff, and who appointed it (Micah 6:9) — and the meaning is: every place over which this staff passes, <small>(and likewise the staff)</small> which YHWH lays upon it, it shall not be for exertion, but rather He shall strike, and the striker is the angel, rejoicing as with timbrels and lyres:" "<b>And in battles of waving.</b> A waving of the hand, to play:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The lemma quotes Isaiah 30:32; the phrase מוסדה is grammatically difficult and rendered hyper-literally per the instruction not to smooth textual obscurity."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:10.337733112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}